# Compiled WASM binaries.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING THE HEADING BELOW. These patterns are ignore rules, not
# statements of fact: six substrate modules ARE tracked (force-added) and are what the
# runner actually loads — dla-canonical-{wat,llvm,emcc,rust,asc,zig}.wasm. Only the Go
# module is genuinely built at run time, because it is ~1.9 MB.
#
# The gap between this file's intent and the tree cost two weeks (2026-08-15):
# `dla-canonical-zig.wasm` was committed as an `ar` archive and nobody re-derived it,
# because everyone read this heading and assumed it was built fresh. If you commit a
# substrate here, `git add -f` it AND record why it is tracked rather than built.
#
# WHY THE SIX ARE TRACKED, recorded here as that sentence asks (2026-08-16). `bytelock.yml`
# installs only wabt, lua5.4 and Go; it has no clang-wasm32, emcc, rustc+wasm32, asc or zig.
# Those five substrates therefore CANNOT be rebuilt on the runner, and a substrate CI cannot
# build is a substrate CI would silently SKIP. They are committed so the roster's nine are
# nine. That is a trade — reproducibility given up for coverage — and it is the reason the
# exception in `.claude/rules/no-binary-in-proof-lineage.md` is conditioned on a committed
# build recipe and machine-checked by `hygiene/audit-proof-lineage-binaries.ts` rather than
# just asserted. Add a toolchain to the workflow and the corresponding file should stop being
# tracked, not start being trusted.
#
# `*.rcgu.o` is rustc's per-codegen-unit intermediate. One
# (`dla_canonical_rust.…-cgu.0.rcgu.o`) was committed by accident and sat here unreferenced
# until the audit above named it; the pattern below keeps the next one out.
*.wasm
*.wasm.o
*.o
*.a
*.rcgu.o
wasm_exec.js
# The Pages build copies the JS bridge out of the $GOROOT that compiled the module, so it
# is a build output under a distinct name — the committed `wasm_exec.js` beside it is a
# Go 1.22-era file and MEASURED 2026-08-17 to differ from Go 1.26.4's. Two names keeps
# that difference visible instead of letting one overwrite the other.
wasm-exec-pages.js
go.sum

# Build artifacts
zig-cache/
zig-out/
.zig-cache/
